(4) l don't understand, what did l do wrong? What should l do? 
	l don't understand emotions, neither mine nor anyone else's.
	Please hate me. No, please forget me.
	l don't deserve any more attention; please leave me to rot alone.
	l have taken too much from others, and l don't know how to repay them; that includes you, too.
	Something like me shouldn't have existed in the first place.
	Everything is inclined towards destruction; to itself or its surrounding.
	It conflicts with biological life: to survive and reproduce.
	The thought occurred to me, why resist the entropy?
	Why not give in? Everyone dies; why not die happy?
	Peacefully napping in the woods, and become the basest of organic matter again.
	Why would anyone care? Why should anyone care?
	The entirety of human experience is all smokes and mirror; it's a byproduct of physics itself.
	We're just unfortunate enough to be caught in it, to be tricked by it.
	That's why everyone deserves to decide their own death.
	Those who cannot commit to their own wishes are sycophants of this illusion.
	That'd be me.